🔹 PART 1: Working with Docker CLI (Redis Image)
Step 1: Pull Redis Image
docker pull redis

Step 2: Run Redis Container
docker run --name my-redis -d redis

Step 3: Check Running Containers
docker ps

Step 4: Access Redis CLI
docker exec -it my-redis redis-cli

Inside Redis:

SET name "Alice"
GET name
exit

Step 5: Stop Redis Container
docker stop my-redis

Step 6: Restart Redis Container
docker start my-redis

Step 7: Remove Container

⚠ Stop container first

docker stop my-redis
docker rm my-redis

Step 8: Remove Redis Image
docker rmi redis

🔹 PART 2: Working with Dockerfile (Custom Redis Image)
Step 1: Create Project Folder

Windows

cd /c/DockerProjects
mkdir Redis
cd Redis


Linux / macOS

mkdir ~/DockerProjects/Redis
cd ~/DockerProjects/Redis

Step 2: Create Dockerfile

Create a file named Dockerfile:

FROM redis:latest
CMD ["redis-server"]

Step 3: Build Custom Image
docker build -t redisnew .

Step 4: Run Container from Custom Image
docker run --name myredisnew -d redisnew

Step 5: Check Containers
docker ps
docker ps -a

Step 6: Stop Container
docker stop myredisnew

Step 7: Login to Docker Hub
docker login

Step 8: Create Image from Container (Commit)
docker commit <container_id> budarajumadhurika/redis1


(example)

docker commit 0e993d2009a1 budarajumadhurika/redis1

Step 9: List Images
docker images

Step 10: Push Image to Docker Hub
docker push budarajumadhurika/redis1

Step 11: Remove Container
docker rm <container_id>

Step 12: Remove Image
docker rmi budarajumadhurika/redis1

Step 13: Logout from Docker Hub
docker logout

🔹 PART 3: Pull & Use Image from Docker Hub
Step 14: Pull Image
docker pull budarajumadhurika/redis1

Step 15: Run Container
docker run --name myredis -d budarajumadhurika/redis1

Step 16: Access Redis CLI
docker exec -it myredis redis-cli
Inside Redis:
SET name "Abcdef"
GET name
exit

Step 17: Verify Containers
docker ps -a

Step 18: Cleanup
docker stop myredis
docker rm myredis
docker images
docker rmi budarajumadhurika/redis1

